/**
 * TEAM ROSTER — the thirty-three people of the department.
 *
 *   Project Management   — 15 people
 *   Process & Procedures — 11 people
 *   BPT & Testing        —  7 people
 *   TOTAL                — 33 people
 *
 * Names, roles and biographies come from the content workbook by way of
 * `ppmd-content/workbookContent`, which is generated by
 * `scripts/import-content.mjs`. Nothing descriptive is written here.
 *
 * Portraits do NOT come from the workbook: its `photo_filename` column is
 * empty, and the files under `public/people/` are the real photographs.
 * So this module holds one table — id, portrait file — and joins the
 * workbook's content onto it. That join is by workbook id rather than by
 * name on purpose: it is the one thing that stays stable when a name is
 * respelled, and the site ids are also what the spatial compositions seat
 * people by.
 *
 * Some of the workbook's descriptive columns are still sample text. The
 * importer withholds those, so those records simply arrive without a
 * biography and every surface already omits a field it is not given. A
 * profile then shows the portrait, the name, the role and the team —
 * which is what is actually known about that person.
 *
 * The Senior Director and the Senior Manager who leads the department
 * live in leadershipData.ts and are NOT part of this roster.
 */
import { WB_PEOPLE } from '../ppmd-content/workbookContent'
import type { Person, PersonLevel } from './peopleTypes'
import { PORTRAIT_FOCUS } from './portraitFraming'

